<p class="foot">Values are standard reference figures at 1 atm: melting and boiling points in kelvin, density at room temperature, electronegativity on the Pauling scale. Properties of elements 104 to 118 and some past fermium are predicted or estimated. Neutron counts use the most common isotope, approximately. The shells, orbital clouds and lattices are schematic, not to scale. Ionization energies, electron affinities, abundances and hazards are rounded reference values; the isotope stability check and decay chains are simplified. Shortcuts: <kbd>&larr;</kbd> <kbd>&rarr;</kbd> step through elements (with a tile focused, arrows move around the table), <kbd>/</kbd> search, <kbd>S</kbd> switch 3D or scribbles, <kbd>D</kbd> pencil tool, <kbd>Esc</kbd> stop the quiz or pencil.</p>
